      "sourceTextSha256": "581b6c4dc64912cefc7cc4bffe94162fc956054f07f8096a22798092838a8faf",
      "text": "Day 7 · Breakfast, then a 3-hour city tour of Buenos Aires with an English-speaking guide: La Boca; San Telmo and the antiques market of Plaza Dorrego; the Plaza de Mayo and the Casa Rosada, linked to the memory of Eva Perón; the 67-metre Obelisk on Avenida 9 de Julio, one of the widest avenues in the world; Recoleta and its famous cemetery; and modern Puerto Madero. In the evening, a tango show with dinner (without a guide), born in the port districts among immigrants and gauchos, with traditional dishes and fine Argentine wines.",
